usage: deploy_source030.py [-h]
                           --mode {static-stage,static-preflight,boundary-prepare,launch}
                           --run-root RUN_ROOT
                           --old-source-root OLD_SOURCE_ROOT
                           --new-source-root NEW_SOURCE_ROOT
                           --source-archive SOURCE_ARCHIVE
                           --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT
                           --source-archive-sha256 SOURCE_ARCHIVE_SHA256
                           [--controller-intent CONTROLLER_INTENT]
                           [--controller-receipt-sha256 CONTROLLER_RECEIPT_SHA256]
                           [--runtime-script RUNTIME_SCRIPT]

Explicit local-to-Kaiser deployment steps. No SSH, signals, polling or
scheduler. static-stage/preflight can run while source029 trains. boundary-
prepare requires the real completed-speed controller receipt and archived,
exited old wrapper. Only the separately invoked launch mode submits the
existing native wrapper. Every ambiguous mutation intent is retained and must
be inspected, never retried.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --mode {static-stage,static-preflight,boundary-prepare,launch}
  --run-root RUN_ROOT
  --old-source-root OLD_SOURCE_ROOT
  --new-source-root NEW_SOURCE_ROOT
  --source-archive SOURCE_ARCHIVE
  --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT
  --source-archive-sha256 SOURCE_ARCHIVE_SHA256
  --controller-intent CONTROLLER_INTENT
  --controller-receipt-sha256 CONTROLLER_RECEIPT_SHA256
  --runtime-script RUNTIME_SCRIPT
